IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Limited hospitalization indemnity policy`

-- Isomorphic encoding of the attached policy wording (fixtures/chubb-policy.txt).
-- This file defines RULES ONLY -- no claim data. Per-claim facts are supplied
-- by the caller (see apply.l4), as values of the Hospitalization record below.
--
-- Two simplifications, both mandated by the task brief rather than chosen here:
--
-- 1. The agreement is always assumed signed and the premium always assumed
--    paid on time, so items 1 and 2 of Section 1.1 are not encoded as
--    separate rules at all -- there is nothing to check.
--
-- 2. Every date/time fact about a claim -- other than the claimant's age --
--    is expressed as a NUMBER of months elapsed since the policy's effective
--    date, rather than as a calendar DATE. Consequently no rule below ever
--    needs to compute the interval between two dates: each temporal check is
--    a direct comparison of a given "months after effective date" figure
--    against a fixed deadline drawn straight from the contract text (6, 7,
--    or 12 months after the effective date).
--
-- A further, implicit simplification: every Hospitalization value already
-- represents "hospitalization for sickness or accidental injury" per the
-- opening words of Section 1.1 -- that gate is definitional (it is what the
-- record type means), not a separate BOOLEAN flag to be toggled.

§§ `The facts a claim brings`

DECLARE Hospitalization HAS
    `age at hospitalization`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `hospitalization months after effective date`                       IS A NUMBER
    `wellness visit confirmation submitted months after effective date` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `wellness visit occurred months after effective date`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `fraud committed`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `misrepresentation committed`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `material information withheld`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by skydiving`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by military service`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by firefighting service`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by police service`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Section 1 Policy in effect and conditions`

§§ `1.3 the wellness visit condition`

-- "No later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective date ... you
-- will supply us with written confirmation from the medical provider ... of
-- a wellness visit ... occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary of
-- the effective date." Two separate deadlines: the written confirmation
-- must be SUBMITTED by month 7; the visit it attests to must have OCCURRED
-- by month 6. Both figures are "MAYBE NUMBER" on the claim because, as of
-- the moment being assessed, either event may simply not have happened yet
-- -- in which case the condition is "still pending", not yet failed.

`confirmation submission deadline in months` MEANS 7

`wellness visit deadline in months` MEANS 6

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wellness visit is not known to be late` IF
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit occurred months after effective date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST t  THEN t AT MOST `wellness visit deadline in months`

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wellness confirmation was submitted in time, or not yet due` IF
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit confirmation submitted months after effective date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST t  THEN t AT MOST `confirmation submission deadline in months`

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1.3 is still pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` IF
    `the wellness confirmation was submitted in time, or not yet due` claim
    AND `the wellness visit is not known to be late` claim

§§ `1.2 cancelation`

-- "Cancelation will be deemed to have occurred if there is fraud, or any
-- misrepresentation or material withholding of any information ... or if
-- the condition set out in Section 1.3 has not been satisfied in a timely
-- fashion. It will also be automatically canceled at midnight ... on the
-- last day of the policy term described in Section 5" -- the policy term
-- itself is the one-year period fixed by Section 3.6 below.

`policy term in months` MEANS 12

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cancelation is deemed to have occurred` IF
    claim's `fraud committed`
    OR claim's `misrepresentation committed`
    OR claim's `material information withheld`
    OR NOT `section 1.3 is still pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion` claim
    OR claim's `hospitalization months after effective date` AT LEAST `policy term in months`

§§ `1.1 policy in effect`

-- "The policy will be in effect if: 1. This agreement is signed, 2. The
-- applicable premium ... has been paid, and 3. The condition set out in
-- Section 1.3 is still pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion,
-- and 4. The policy has not been canceled." Items 1 and 2 are assumed true
-- throughout per the task brief (see file header) and so have no rule here;
-- item 3 is folded into `cancelation is deemed to have occurred` above,
-- alongside item 4, since 1.2 cancels the policy precisely when item 3
-- fails.

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` IF
    NOT `cancelation is deemed to have occurred` claim

§ `Section 2 General exclusions`

-- "Your policy will not apply to ... any event causing sickness or
-- accidental injury arising directly or indirectly out of: 1. Skydiving; or
-- 2. Service in the military; or 3. Service as a fire fighter; or 4.
-- Service in the police; or 5. If your age at the time of the
-- hospitalization is equal to or greater than 80 years of age." Note that
-- exclusions 1-4 require the hospitalization to ARISE OUT OF the named
-- activity -- merely holding that occupation, or being on duty, at the time
-- of an unrelated injury does not by itself trigger the exclusion.

`excluded age threshold` MEANS 80

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hospitalization arises directly or indirectly out of an excluded activity` IF
    claim's `caused by skydiving`
    OR claim's `caused by military service`
    OR claim's `caused by firefighting service`
    OR claim's `caused by police service`

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is excluded by age` IF
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST `excluded age threshold`

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general exclusion applies` IF
    `the hospitalization arises directly or indirectly out of an excluded activity` claim
    OR `the claimant is excluded by age` claim

§ `Section 3 General conditions`

§§ `3.1 where the policy applies`

-- "Your Policy insures You twenty-four (24) hours a day anywhere in the
-- world." There is no place-of-loss or time-of-day restriction, so this
-- condition can never cause a claim to fail. It is included as an explicit
-- always-true fact for completeness and traceability against the source
-- text, rather than silently omitted.

`the policy applies regardless of place or time of day` MEANS TRUE

-- Sections 3.2 (arbitration and the 60-day pre-suit waiting period), 3.3
-- (governing law), 3.4 (currency of payment) and 3.5 (timing of premium
-- payment, already assumed satisfied per the task brief) are procedural or
-- administrative terms. They govern how a dispute is resolved or how
-- payment is made, not whether a given hospitalization is within the scope
-- of coverage, so they are not encoded as gating conditions on `covered`
-- below.

-- 3.6 (Policy Term) fixes the one-year term used by `policy term in months`
-- above, in Section 1.2.

§ `Top level coverage decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Hospitalization
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE covered IF
    `the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim
    AND NOT `a general exclusion applies` claim
    AND `the policy applies regardless of place or time of day`
